The attached image displays flow cytometry histograms showing the expression of costimulatory molecules CD40, CD80, and CD86 on bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) after two days of incubation. The black line represents BMDCs treated with 250 µg/mL Nano-11, while the gray line represents untreated control cells. The histograms demonstrate that Nano-11 markedly increased the expression of CD80 and CD86, and slightly increased CD40, compared to the control. This indicates that Nano-11 activates dendritic cells, a crucial function for an effective vaccine adjuvant to promote an immune response, as discussed in the surrounding text.